# evidence/startup-A: how the image-A start-up data of fuzz_disco is re-derived: proofs/libreac/fuzz_disco/lib/A/{AB01,AB03,AB05,AB12,AD2i,AD2j,AD1k,ACej}.v. proves no function (kind: measurement).
# One line per file: path (relative to this directory), kind, sha256, role. kind: script = a script written for this evidence (a driver, a check, an extract); input = a file a script reads; table = a per-value table a script writes; gate = a gate or comparison record a script writes. Written by mk_manifest.py.
# Re-run: bash run.sh REPO IMAGE DONOR_IMAGE TOOLS OUT, with REPO a checkout of this tree, the two released images fuzz_disco.asan (sha256 5e39150dd810...) and cgif_file_fuzzer.asan (sha256 7093581aab04...) of index/binaries.tsv, and TOOLS a directory holding the tools run here at the paths tools.sha256 names. It checks every tool's sha256, regenerates every table and gate record under tables/ (cmp) and compares each regenerated .v file with the shipped one (the compare.py records under tables/, cmp). Measured on 2026-10-31: every comparison holds.
# Tools: not shipped here, cited. Of record (internal record): the start-up set 2026-10-30d (hsform, plantail, atable, gen_ad2, gen_ad1k, pins, keyset, af0m, jtsites, wh8, pautrlen/rvdis) and rvelf (pg-reloc-portcore e0e94a04094b). The others: itabranges.py (indexed as found, not of record: tools/startup-cited/itabranges/563d9c175a38/ at registry commit 5fd6732f0003, sha256 563d9c175a38); binmatch_plan.py and imgref.py (copy as found, not of record: the tools that produced the AB05 plan body, tools/startup-cited/binmatch_plan/7f058fcb8e4a/ at registry commit 5fd6732f0003, sha256 7f058fcb8e4a, 064874159929); gen_traces.py (indexed as found, not of record: tools/startup-cited/gen_traces/59966c883510/ at registry commit 5fd6732f0003, sha256 59966c883510); resolve_code.py (indexed as found, not of record: tools/startup-cited/resolve_code/81803218fe79/ at registry commit 5fd6732f0003, sha256 81803218fe79). tools.sha256 has each one's path and sha256. No tool is edited: what a run here needs that a tool does not do (read the twin listing where it read the twin, take an input where it names a host path) is done by a driver under drivers/, which imports the tool unchanged from TOOLS, replaces the one function or constant, and runs the tool's own __main__ block. The unstripped twin is not shipped: twin/fuzz_disco.asan.syms carries the symbol facts the tools read.
# Every tool tools.sha256 names, and ColA.v, is kept byte-equal at its former path in this directory on the internal records ref records/libreac-fuzz_disco-1031-tool-copies.
# What ships beyond the tools' output (the compare.py records): the notice line 4 of AB01, AB03, AB05 (the set's hsform refuses that text, it names the collector's lane); AB05's module paths; AB12's six header lines and its stops_more (12 of the image's 13 self-loops, the 13th 0x6eca0 left out under the KEEP ruling for start-up tables; TFIB_TEXT_N 112639 is the tool's value); the lia hook line of AD2i (line 17) and AD1k (line 16), the text zifyhook.py (indexed as found, not of record: tools/startup-cited/zifyhook/db7fa393c85e/ at registry commit 5fd6732f0003, sha256 db7fa393c85e) writes; whether that tool or a hand edit wrote it is not recorded (no numeral); AD2i's w_H8 notice, H1_8 comment and two proof steps (written by hand at the commit; no numeral); ACej's template text and its three harness contexts 0x80c04, 0x80c28, 0x80e50 (the return addresses of the harness calls: traces/call_sites.py lists them).
# Read, not derived here: proofs/libreac/fuzz_disco/lib/A/AF0m.v (owned cells; evidence/core-A) by atable --cells, gen_ad2 and gen_ad1k, and proofs/libreac/fuzz_disco/lib/A/AB1h.v (segments) by gen_ad2; both give the shipped outputs. No derivation to re-run: AB1m and its parts (the donor's statement text; its numerals are checker inputs the kernel evaluates), and the hand numerals of AB13, AB1h, AB1k, AD1g (kernel computations over the image; base text from the core relocation, evidence/core-A).
# Not re-run here: the collector build that printed the dumps (needs the donor tree built on a build VM); the function pairing plan/binmatch.cgif.asan.json (made from both images and the twin by binmatch_disco.py (indexed as found, not of record: tools/startup-cited/binmatch_disco/a28d0565b394/ at registry commit 5fd6732f0003, sha256 a28d0565b394), not shipped). Gate records of earlier runs are not shipped: the gates are re-run on the released images in evidence/gates-A.
